# `go build ./...` in this directory writes a binary named after the module.
# The wrapper always compiles a fresh temporary binary from source, so this
# artifact is never used — and it is a ~3.5 MiB platform-specific executable that
# Linux CI cannot run. Ignore it so a `git add` of this directory cannot sweep it
# into the tree, which is exactly how it got committed once.
/comment-disclosure-drift
